{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01026",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 3.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Afternoon, thanks for coming in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.68,
      "end_seconds": 6.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Hi, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.12,
      "end_seconds": 9.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.96,
      "end_seconds": 21.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, it's a cut on my finger. It's getting on my nerves now. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.5,
      "end_seconds": 24.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Alright, since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.36,
      "end_seconds": 28.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Since Friday, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.43,
      "end_seconds": 34.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.98,
      "end_seconds": 50.49,
      "duration_seconds": 15.51,
      "text": "It's worse with gripping. Pressure helps a bit. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.49,
      "end_seconds": 54.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.36,
      "end_seconds": 69.36,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "A numb fingertip goes along with it, most of the time. The numb fingertip? That's been since last weekend. About numb fingertip, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.32,
      "end_seconds": 85.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Have you had any pus or bite?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.86,
      "end_seconds": 89.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "No, no pus or bite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.44,
      "end_seconds": 94.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Have you noticed weakness of the hand or redness spreading?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.67,
      "end_seconds": 101.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Let me think, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.73,
      "end_seconds": 107.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "So, your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.05,
      "end_seconds": 111.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.46,
      "end_seconds": 115.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.27,
      "end_seconds": 120.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.22,
      "end_seconds": 124.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.76,
      "end_seconds": 128.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.63,
      "end_seconds": 132.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.46,
      "end_seconds": 136.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.84,
      "end_seconds": 139.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.84,
      "end_seconds": 144.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.88,
      "end_seconds": 151.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.89,
      "end_seconds": 154.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.74,
      "end_seconds": 168.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Right, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.54,
      "end_seconds": 180.79,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol. I have diabetes, for nearly five years. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.16,
      "end_seconds": 189.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear. Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.11,
      "end_seconds": 195.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "It's metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.45,
      "end_seconds": 202.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Okay, time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.05,
      "end_seconds": 216.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.61,
      "end_seconds": 243.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 108 over 71, pulse is 85 beats a minute. And SpO2 99 percent on room air, respiratory rate 14."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.34,
      "end_seconds": 250.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.78,
      "end_seconds": 259.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.5,
      "end_seconds": 262.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.66,
      "end_seconds": 287.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre clean cut over the first knuckle, the finger moves fully and the fingertip feels normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.71,
      "end_seconds": 307.15,
      "duration_seconds": 16.44,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Putting it all together, I don't have a clear answer today: a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury is possible, and so is a tendon injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.09,
      "end_seconds": 311.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I mean, is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.19,
      "end_seconds": 327.53,
      "duration_seconds": 14.34,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury, and we'll know more once the an X-ray of the finger is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.18,
      "end_seconds": 376.55,
      "duration_seconds": 32.37,
      "text": "I'm going to order an X-ray of the finger, for laceration. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. We'll begin with tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once, for one day. That should help with tetanus prevention. Keep the dressing dry for two days and watch for redness or pus. I'd like you back if it looks infected. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.14,
      "end_seconds": 390.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "So, I take the tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once and come back if it looks infected. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.96,
      "end_seconds": 394.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.83,
      "end_seconds": 397.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.07,
      "end_seconds": 400.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}